# KiKi FM currently needs NO environment variables or secrets.
#
# All data (stations, categories) lives in src/data/stations.json and
# ships as part of the static build. Favorites live in the visitor's
# browser (localStorage). There is no API key, database URL, or
# analytics token to configure.
#
# This file exists so the pattern is ready if you add something later
# (e.g. an analytics site ID, or a form-submission endpoint). When you
# do, add the variable here with a placeholder value, and Vite will
# pick up a real .env file (which must NOT be committed) automatically
# for any variable prefixed with VITE_.
#
# Example (not currently used):
# VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=
